.TH FIRST-CONTACT 8 "2026-11-12" "first-contact 1.0.1" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
first-contact \- Postfix milter that flags first-time senders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B first-contact
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR]
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B first-contact
is a Postfix milter that adds an
.B X-First-Contact
header when a recipient receives a message for the first time from a sender,
or when a known sender returns after a long absence.
It can also insert a visible warning at the top of the message text.
.PP
The milter never stops mail delivery: on error it answers
.B CONTINUE
and the header alone is added when the visible warning cannot be applied.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the milter. Normally started by
.BR first-contact-milter.service .
Requires
.BR pymilter .
.TP
.B check
Report whether a sender is new for a recipient, without sending mail.
.TP
.B list
List stored contacts.
.TP
.B stats
Print database statistics: pairs, senders, recipients and messages.
.TP
.B prune
Delete contacts older than the given number of days.
.TP
.B simulate
Show the header and the visible warning that would be added to a message.
.TP
.B doctor
Check configuration, database, socket, Postfix settings, milter order,
banner and whitelist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Configuration file. Default:
.IR /etc/first-contact/config.ini .
.SH "CHECK OPTIONS"
.TP
.BI \-\-sender " address"
Envelope sender.
.TP
.BI \-\-recipient " address"
Envelope recipient.
.TP
.BI \-\-client " ip"
SMTP client IP address, used for CIDR whitelist checks.
.TP
.B \-\-from-header
Interpret the
.B \-\-sender
value as a
.B From:
header value.
.SH "LIST OPTIONS"
.TP
.BI \-\-sender " filter"
Filter by sender.
.TP
.BI \-\-recipient " filter"
Filter by recipient.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " number"
Maximum number of rows.
.TP
.BI \-\-offset " number"
Skip the first rows.
.SH "PRUNE OPTIONS"
.TP
.BI \-\-days " number"
Delete contacts not seen for this many days. Defaults to
.BR retention_days .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be deleted without changing the database.
.SH "SIMULATE OPTIONS"
.TP
.BI \-\-eml " file"
RFC 5322 message to examine.
.TP
.BI \-\-sender " address"
Envelope sender. Defaults to the
.B From:
header.
.TP
.BI \-\-recipient " address"
Envelope recipient. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-client " ip"
SMTP client IP address.
.TP
.BI \-\-helo " name"
SMTP HELO/EHLO name.
.TP
.BI \-\-known\-days " number"
Pretend the contact happened this many days ago, to test the dormant-sender
rule.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " file"
Database to use. Defaults to a temporary file; the real database is not
touched.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses the INI format.
Section
.B [milter]
sets the socket, header name and header position;
.B [banner]
sets the warning mode, text, subject prefix and limits;
.B [whitelist]
lists excluded senders and networks;
.B [policy]
controls scope, dormant sender detection and observation mode;
.B [store]
sets the SQLite path and retention;
.B [logging]
sets log level and syslog output.
.PP
After changing the configuration, restart the service:
.B systemctl restart first-contact-milter
.PP
Whitelist files are re-read automatically when they change.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/first-contact/config.ini
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/first-contact/whitelist.txt
Whitelist, one entry per line.
.TP
.I /var/lib/first-contact/contacts.db
SQLite contact database.
.TP
.I /var/spool/postfix/first-contact/milter.sock
Unix socket used by Postfix (inside the Postfix chroot).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/first-contact-milter.service
Systemd service unit.
.SH NOTES
The milter must be appended to
.B smtpd_milters
in
.IR /etc/postfix/main.cf .
.PP
The body banner is inserted into existing
.B text/plain
and
.B text/html
parts; it does not create attachments.
It invalidates the sender's DKIM signatures for the modified message.
Use
.B [banner] mode = off
to leave the body untouched.
.PP
Messages that are
.B multipart/signed
or
.B multipart/encrypted
are not rewritten.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime or database error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
Missing dependency.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR postfix (1),
.BR postconf (1),
.BR master (5),
.BR systemd.unit (5)
